    "final_answer": "Updated `settlement_reconcile.py` to use the v2 GraphQL API.\n\nChanges:\n- Switched from `/v1/graphql` to `/v2/graphql`.\n- Added cursor pagination using `pageInfo.endCursor` and `hasNextPage`.\n- Continues through short and empty pages instead of stopping early.\n- Deduplicates by settlement `id`, keeping the last received version.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After`, resending the identical request.\n- Restarts from the beginning when the server rejects an expired/malformed cursor.\n- Kept the CLI and output format unchanged.\n\nVerified against the v2 server at `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n- Traversed 27 pages, including 13 short and 4 empty pages.\n- Received 1,892 deliveries representing 1,873 unique settlements; 19 were amended/redelivered.\n- Output has **1,873 lines, 1,873 unique IDs, no duplicates**.\n- ID set matches both v2 and v1.\n- Output values match the last delivered v2 version for every settlement.\n- Output is exactly identical to v1 in order and content: `st_00001` through `st_01873`.\n\nAlso exercised the retry and cursor-restart paths against a mock server; both passed.",
